  "id": "Compound::DB00757 - Gene::1559",
  "verbalization": "Dolasetron is implicated in the regulation of Cyp2c9 through multiple indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that Dolasetron binds to Cyp3a4 and Cyp2d6, which are both involved in oxidative metabolism, and that these enzymes are part of the Cyp2c9 family. This implies a potential functional link between Dolasetron and Cyp2c9, possibly through shared metabolic pathways. Additionally, the inclusion of Dolasetron in the class of serotonin 3 receptor antagonists, which includes Alosetron, further suggests a broader pharmacological context. While the direct interaction between Dolasetron and Cyp2c9 is not explicitly stated, the indirect pathways through Cyp3a4 and Cyp2d6 provide a plausible mechanism for the observed relationship. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of enzyme participation in mediating drug effects, underscoring the importance of enzyme-catalyzed reactions in drug metabolism and action.",
